  "viewer_notes": [
    "One CT case, source metadata age 90.00 and sex female; study type is ct pelvis, trauma/abdomen. This is not a dedicated neck CT, a normal thyroid atlas, ultrasound acquisition or the patient being reported.",
    "All eight original reviewed source label interfaces and all 52,040 triangles retained. The thyroid remains two disconnected source components; no invented isthmus bridge. Both common-carotid source boundaries retain 22 open edges each. Closed label ends are not physical anatomical endpoints.",
    "Declared source grid 255\u00d7255\u00d7523, 1.5 mm sample pitch, RAS sform preserved. Raw DICOM calibration, native contrast phase, effective tiny-wall resolution and independent patient orientation remain unverified. Camera labels use source coordinates.",
    "No smoothing, capping, padding, decimation, component removal, relabelling or fitted registration. Original voxel stair steps and three ambiguity-resolution field residuals remain. Display colours are not photographic tissue colours.",
    "Capsule, isthmus continuity, parathyroids, recurrent laryngeal nerves, fine arteries/veins, lymph nodes, nodule internal tissues and every adjacent wall/interface are not independently resolved. These are partial source labels, not complete thyroid reporting anatomy.",
    "Source CT and annotations supply no ultrasound echogenicity, Doppler, salivary/airway function, pathological tissue identity, diagnostic classifier or registration with the published ultrasound examples.",
    "ZIP member CRCs and local SHA256s were verified with stable publisher size/checksum before and after range acquisition. The whole 37.4 GB archive MD5 was not verified and no HTTP entity tag was supplied. Independent anatomical/clinical approval remains pending. Jakob Wasserthal. TotalSegmentator dataset v3.0.0, case s0358. DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22688904. CC BY 4.0. Adaptation: original 0.5 label-interface extraction, float32 transport and display normals."
  ],
